{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicGeodesicZAxisUniqueness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicGeodesicZAxisUniqueness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicGeodesic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicGeodesicZAxis","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HyperbolicMetricSeparation"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.zaxis_minimizer_eq_vseg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.zaxis_minimizer_eq_vseg","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxisUniqueness.lean#L91-L339","doc":"**WALL-4 — z-axis geodesic uniqueness (DERIVED).**  A constant-speed\nminimiser between two z-axis points is pointwise the vertical segment `vseg`.\nThe genuine equality-case of the FTC vertical lower bound.\n\nThis does NOT close the full `HypMinimizerUnique` conjecture (arbitrary\nendpoints): no instance is fabricated; only the z-axis case is derived. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.horiz_zero_of_norm_eq_abs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.horiz_zero_of_norm_eq_abs","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HyperbolicGeodesicZAxisUniqueness.lean#L75-L89","doc":"**`‖v‖ = |v 2|` collapses the horizontal velocity.**  In `ℝ³` (Euclidean),\nif the norm of `v` equals the absolute value of its height component, the two\nhorizontal components vanish: `‖v‖² = Σ (v i)² = (v 2)²` forces\n`(v 0)² + (v 1)² = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}